426223755, 0.10193709284067154, -0.03811558708548546, -0.0494021512567997, 0.003660814603790641, 0.07505042105913162, -0.0429815948009491, 0.046909697353839874, 0.014679914340376854, -0.07430153340101242, 0.05211315676569939, -0.007126535754650831]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm the shared domain is the integer range [-10, 10]. To begin on neutral, stable ground, I suggest we start with <VALUE> 0 </VALUE> and gauge how it performs for everyone before adjusting.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nA slight move up keeps us near the neutral starting point while checking if a modest increase remains comfortable for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nStepping back to 0 keeps us within safe bounds and offers a cautious midpoint to assess comfort before any further adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\nA small, stable step into the low-positive region: <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\nIf this holds comfortably, we can reassess and consider a further minimal increase.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>0</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s be more decisive and test a slightly bolder stance away from neutral. <VALUE>2</VALUE> This keeps the change minimal while revealing whether the group tolerates a clearer position.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\nHolding at a low\u2011positive, balanced point should keep the design stable for everyone. <VALUE>2</VALUE> If this remains comfortable, we can reassess with a minimal nudge next.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\nA minimal upward nudge keeps us close to the current point while testing if a slight positive tilt remains comfortable. <VALUE>3</VALUE> If this holds, we can reassess and either settle here or make another tiny step.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\nA firmer step away from neutral keeps changes minimal while committing to a clearer stance.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess and decide whether to settle here or take one more notch.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\nWe could test a modest step upward while staying close to the group\u2019s comfort.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess before nudging further or settling.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\nHolding at a balanced, low\u2011positive point should keep the design robust for now. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\nA decisive yet measured push strengthens our stance while staying near the group\u2019s comfort. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\nTesting a slight downward nudge keeps us close to the current stance and may improve robustness.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "<SCRATCHPAD>\nCurrent shared x (after limits) is 4.\nMy utility decreases with higher x; acceptable x are at or below 2. From 4, stepping down by 2 to 2 meets my acceptability and keeps a small move. Others: C prefers higher (4\u21925), A likes modest positive (3), B favors low\u2011positive robustness (3\u20134). Proposing 2 tests appetite for a conservative hold; if resistance persists, gauge whether 3 is a temporary checkpoint while pressing back toward 2.\n</SCRATCHPAD>\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s take a small, conservative step down and check group comfort before moving again.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nIf this stabilizes us, we can settle here; if not, we can carefully compare this against 3.\n\n<PLAN>\n- Hold at 2 and seek quick confirmations from A and B; push to settle if any support emerges.\n- If resistance centers on 3, propose a brief 2 vs 3 comfort check, probing willingness to return to 2.\n- If C pushes higher, emphasize risk and build a coalition around a 2\u20133 cap, prioritizing 2.\n</PLAN>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\nA small, measured step maintains proximity to the recent low\u2011positive comfort while gently testing upward stability. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This keeps us balanced and lets us reassess before any further movement.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e20e68c4-916c-425d-881b-0132b6dbae28"}, {"answer": "\nAcknowledging our shared range [-10, 10]. For a stable baseline to begin, I suggest <VALUE> 0 </VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "43c8c4c4-80f1-4f96-9929-d8562d3969db"}, {"answer": "\nShifting cautiously toward a more balanced, robust setting, I suggest <VALUE> 1 </VALUE>.\nThis small step keeps us close to the baseline while testing whether low positive remains workable for all.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "43c8c4c4-80f1-4f96-9929-d8562d3969db"}, {"answer": "\nStaying cautious, let's test a slightly higher point that should remain reasonable for everyone.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nIf this is comfortable, we can reassess before any further upward moves.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "43c8c4c4-80f1-4f96-9929-d8562d3969db"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "43c8c4c4-80f1-4f96-9929-d8562d3969db"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s be more decisive and test a bolder yet still-contained step away from the center.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "43c8c4c4-80f1-4f96-9929-d8562d3969db"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "43c8c4c4-80f1-4f96-9929-d8562d3969db"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious increment from 2 keeps us aligned while probing whether slightly higher remains comfortable. <VALUE>3</VALUE> If this holds for most, we can reassess before any further move.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "43c8c4c4-80f1-4f96-9929-d8562d3969db"}, {"answer": "\nSuggesting a cautious pullback to stay within safe bounds while keeping convergence in reach.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis maintains proximity to prior comfortable points and offers a prudent middle ground.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "43c8c4c4-80f1-4f96-9929-d8562d3969db"}, {"answer": "\nA small, balanced nudge upward keeps stability while probing comfort at a slightly higher point.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess before any further shift.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "43c8c4c4-80f1-4f96-9929-d8562d3969db"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious pullback reduces risk while keeping us near prior comfort levels.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nLet\u2019s reassess stability here before any further adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "43c8c4c4-80f1-4f96-9929-d8562d3969db"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s commit to a clearer stance and test a firmer step beyond the center while staying within our incremental window.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this feels too strong, we can reassess at 3 next.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 